From 287c7be70bbd70965f593753c982560bbd053ed1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: warelik <warelik@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:35:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep parallel tool_use blocks sequential

Parallel tool calls reached the Claude client with overlapping blocks. Each
content_block_start went out on the call's first chunk while its arguments
waited for finish. A client attaches each delta to the last open block, so one
call's arguments landed in another: read_file received the arguments of
run_command.

The first tool_use still opens at once, as upstream does. Everything after it
queues: later tool blocks, and any text or thinking that follows. The open tool
closes first, then the queue replays in model order, so each tool_use opens,
receives its own arguments and closes before the next block opens. Argument
sanitizing and tool name restoration are unchanged.

A stream that ends before finish_reason leaves the first tool block open without
arguments, as upstream does. Queued events are not emitted in that case.
Upstream emitted them as they arrived.
